      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LUKE SKYWALKER (2) went to the lead last start and did well to hold on for third over 1400m at Gunnedah. Draws to enjoy a soft run in what looks a low-pressure race on paper. No standouts in this field so he gets his chance to finally break through. SHARE OUR SECRET (3) has raced twice this prep and been about the mark on each occasion, the latest over 1400m at Gunnedah where he was just fair through the line. A tongue tie goes on today which could prove to be significant. TARRANT COUNTY (4) caught the eye at his latest outing, a narrow defeat over this course and distance. Seven-year-old maiden who has had plenty of chances but there is still cause for optimism after that latest effort. TURPIN'S TORMENT (5) chalked up a 16th minor placing last start when he stormed home for second over 1700m at Grafton. Not getting too over the top about a 53-start maiden, particularly coming back in trip. Exotics only. ALBERT'S PICK (7) will appreciate the step up in distance and is next in line.",
